{"question_text": {"স্পেশাল বিসিএস (স্বাস্থ্য) - লং কোর্স": [{"id": "1", "question": "১) Example of synovial joint-", "option1": "Symphysis pubis", "option2": "Sacroiliac joint", "option3": "Costovertebral joint", "option4": "Costochondral joint", "answer": "3", "exp": "<strong>Davidson page- 994<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2267.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"968\" height=\"493\" /></strong>"}, {"id": "2", "question": "২) Osteoblasts are-", "option1": "Multinucleated cells", "option2": "Derived from haematopoietic origin", "option3": "Responsible for bone formation ", "option4": "Responsible for bone resorption ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<strong>Davidson page- 992<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2268.jpg\" alt=\"\" /></strong>"}, {"id": "3", "question": "৩) ANA is 100% sensitive for which disease?", "option1": "Rheumatoid arthritis ", "option2": "Sjögren syndrome", "option3": "Mixed connective tissue disease", "option4": "Systemic lupus erythematosus", "answer": "4", "exp": "<strong>Davidson Page 998<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2269.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"926\" height=\"448\" /></strong>"}, {"id": "4", "question": "৪) Anti-RNA polymerase antibody is associated with-", "option1": "Polymyositis", "option2": "Mixed connective tissue disease", "option3": "Diffuse systemic sclerosis", "option4": "Dermatomyositis ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2270.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"924\" height=\"1208\" />"}, {"id": "5", "question": "৫) Which of the following is responsible for pathological fracture?", "option1": "Osteomalacia", "option2": "Osteoporosis ", "option3": "Rheumatoid arthritis ", "option4": "Potts disease ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2271.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "6", "question": "৬) Most common cause of acute low back pain is?", "option1": "Axial spondyloarthritis", "option2": "Vertebral fracture", "option3": "Paget’s disease", "option4": "Mechanical (soft-tissue lesion) back pain", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2272.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "7", "question": "৭) Example of high risk NSAID-", "option1": "Ibuprofen", "option2": "Etoricoxib", "option3": "Indometacin", "option4": "Diclofenac", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2273.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "8", "question": "৮) eGFR monitoring is required during treatment with-", "option1": "Azathioprine", "option2": "Cyclophosphamide ", "option3": "Methotrexate ", "option4": "Sulfasalazine", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2274.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "9", "question": "৯) Most common form of arthritis is-", "option1": "Rheumatoid arthritis ", "option2": "Reactive arthritis ", "option3": "Juvenile idiopathic arthritis ", "option4": "Osteoarthritis ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<strong>Davidson Page 1014<br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2275.jpg\" alt=\"\" /><br /></strong>"}, {"id": "10", "question": "১০) Acute gout is caused due to deposition of-", "option1": "Basic calcium phosphate", "option2": "Calcium pyrophosphate", "option3": "Monosodium urate monohydrate", "option4": "Synthetic crystals ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2277.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "11", "question": "১১) Most common organism responsible for septic arthritis in adults is-", "option1": "Group B streptococcus ", "option2": "Staphylococcus aureus ", "option3": "Neisseria gonorrhoeae", "option4": "E. Coli", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2278.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"836\" height=\"1620\" />"}, {"id": "12", "question": "১২) Hallmark lesion of spondyloarthritis is-", "option1": "Sacroiliitis", "option2": "Osteitis", "option3": "Enthesitis", "option4": "Dactylitis", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2280.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "13", "question": "১৩) Most common extra-articular feature of axial spondyloarthritis?", "option1": "Prostatitis", "option2": "Aortic valve disease ", "option3": "Acute anterior uveitis ", "option4": "Inflammatory bowel disease ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<strong>Davidson Page 1033<br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2282.jpg\" alt=\"\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2281.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1401\" height=\"617\" /><br /></strong>"}, {"id": "14", "question": "১৪) Which antibody is useful in monitoring of SLE?", "option1": "Anti La antibody ", "option2": "Anti Ro antibody", "option3": "Anti dsDNA antibody", "option4": "Antinuclear antibodies", "answer": "3", "exp": "<strong>Davidson Page 999<br /></strong><em>Anti-DNA antibodies bind to double-stranded DNA (dsDNA). They are useful in SLE monitoring as high titres are associated with more severe disease and an increase in antibody titre may precede relapse.</em><strong><br /></strong>"}, {"id": "15", "question": "১৫) Defining feature of osteoarthritis is-", "option1": "Degeneration of articular cartilage", "option2": "Deformity", "option3": "Bony swelling around joint margins", "option4": "Restricted movement due to capsular thickening or blocking by osteophyte", "answer": "1", "exp": "<strong>Davidson Page 1014<br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2276.jpg\" alt=\"\" /><br /></strong>"}, {"id": "16", "question": "১৬) Universal feature of systemic sclerosis is-", "option1": "Arthralgia ", "option2": "Raynaud’s phenomenon", "option3": "Hypertensive renal crisis", "option4": "Erosive esophagitis", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2284.jpg\" alt=\"\" /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2285.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "17", "question": "১৭) Gottron’s papules are seen in-", "option1": "Polymyositis", "option2": "Dermatomyositis ", "option3": "Lichen planus", "option4": "Psoriasis ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<strong>Davidson Page 1043<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2286.jpg\" alt=\"\" /></strong>"}, {"id": "18", "question": "১৮) Positive pathergy test is found in-", "option1": "Giant cell arteritis", "option2": "Sjögren syndrome", "option3": "Behçet’s disease", "option4": "Ankylosing spondylitis ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2287.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "19", "question": "১৯) Osteonecrosis most commonly occurs in-", "option1": "Distal end of tibia", "option2": "Head of the femur", "option3": "Metacarpal bones", "option4": "Calcaneus", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2288.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "20", "question": "২০) Drug induced lupus is caused by-", "option1": "Glucocorticoids ", "option2": "Rifampicin", "option3": "Isoniazid ", "option4": "Ciclosporin", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2289.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "21", "question": "২১) Most common primary bone tumour is-", "option1": "Ewing’s sarcoma", "option2": "Osteosarcoma ", "option3": "Fibrosarcoma", "option4": "Osteoid osteoma", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2290.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1276\" height=\"726\" />"}, {"id": "22", "question": "২২) Characteristic feature of Paget’s disease is-", "option1": "Bone pain", "option2": "Pathological fracture ", "option3": "Deafness", "option4": "Isolated elevation in ALP", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2292.jpg\" alt=\"\" /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2291_OeATsxF.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "23", "question": "২৩) Common adverse effect of Bisphosphonates is-", "option1": "Oesophageal ulceration ", "option2": "Upper GI intolerance ", "option3": "Osteonecrosis of the jaw", "option4": "Atrial fibrillation ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2293.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "24", "question": "২৪) Which of the following skin condition is not seen in systemic lupus erythematosus?", "option1": "Malar rash", "option2": "Discoid rash", "option3": "Heliotrope rash", "option4": "Photosensitive rash", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2294.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "25", "question": "২৫) Which of the following DMARDs must be avoided in pregnancy?", "option1": "Sulfasalazine", "option2": "Azathioprine ", "option3": "Methotrexate ", "option4": "Hydroxichloroquin", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2295.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1193\" height=\"1009\" />"}, {"id": "26", "question": "২৬) Which of the following is not a risk factor for Felty syndrome?", "option1": "Age of onset 50-70 years", "option2": "Seronegative for rheumatoid factor ", "option3": "Long standing rheumatoid arthritis ", "option4": "Female sex", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2296.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "27", "question": "২৭) Most common cause of osteomyelitis in children is-", "option1": "Contiguous spread of infection", "option2": "Sickle cell disease ", "option3": "Haematogenous spread", "option4": "Staph. aureus ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2298.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1059\" height=\"857\" />"}, {"id": "28", "question": "২৮) Usual symptom of fibromyalgia is-", "option1": "Fatiguability", "option2": "Early morning stiffness ", "option3": "Allodynia", "option4": "Distal finger tingling", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2299.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "29", "question": "২৯) Drug that precipitates gout-", "option1": "Thiazide diuretics ", "option2": "Tricyclic antidepressants ", "option3": "Isoniazid ", "option4": "Rifampicin ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2300.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}, {"id": "30", "question": "৩০) Clinical feature of cauda equina syndrome is-", "option1": "Paraesthesia ", "option2": "Saddle anaesthesia ", "option3": "Urinary incontinence ", "option4": "Pain radiates beyond knee", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/IMG_2301.jpg\" alt=\"\" />"}]}, "_source": "archive-question-subject", "_exam_id": 6123, "custom_field": "প্রতি প্রশ্নের মান ১ ও ভুল উত্তরের জন্য ০.৫০ কাটা যাবে।", "exam_time": "1200000", "is_omr": false, "omr_time": "7200000", "examname": "Aug 29, 2024", "type": "BCS-Health-Long", "payment": "BALANCE_NOT"}